==============================================================================
The Author makes the Source Code publicly available subject to the following terms:

(a) INDIVIDUAL RESEARCH & CONTRIBUTION GRANT:
    Subject to the terms herein, an Individual is granted a non-exclusive,
    worldwide, royalty-free license to:
    1. Inspect, audit, and review the Source Code for educational learning,
       security transparency, and non-commercial research.
    2. Modify and adapt the Source Code locally and privately on their own
       personal machine solely for internal experimentation and bug analysis.
    3. Fork the official repository solely for the purpose of submitting bug fixes,
       features, or Pull Requests (PRs) back to the official upstream repository
       (https://github.com/smin987/zipper9).

(b) STRICT PROHIBITION ON MODIFICATION BY COMMERCIAL & CORPORATE USERS:
    Commercial entities, corporations, companies, for-profit organizations/associations,
    and any users acting on their behalf (collectively, "Corporate Entity & Commercial User")
    are strictly PROHIBITED from modifying, altering, patching, or adapting the Source Code,
    whether for internal corporate/business use, evaluation, or external deployment.
    Commercial entities and enterprise users may only execute and deploy the unmodified,
    official Compiled Binaries.

(c) STRICT PROHIBITION ON COMPETING SOFTWARE:
    Neither Individuals nor Corporate Entities & Commercial Users may use the Source Code, in whole
    or in part, modified or unmodified, directly or indirectly, to create,
    develop, market, distribute, release, or license any Competing Product or
    archival service, whether offered for free or for commercial gain.

(d) PROHIBITION ON PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION OF FORKS:
    Public distribution, publishing, hosting, mirroring, or transferring of
    modified Source Code or third-party derivative builds is prohibited without
    the express prior written consent of the Author.

(e) PROHIBITION ON RESALE:
    You may NOT sublicense, rent, lease, sell, or monetize the Source Code.

